    "response": "{\n  \"explanation\": \"The alert indicates a potential SQL Injection vulnerability in the line `resultSet = sqlStatement.executeQuery(\\\"select * from users where name='\\\"+data+\\\"'\\\");`. The variable `data` is directly concatenated into the SQL query string, which can be influenced by external input. The source of `data` is from reading a property file (`../common/config.properties`) using `properties.getProperty(\\\"data\\\")`, which suggests that user-controlled data could potentially be included in the SQL query. Since the data is not bound to placeholders and directly concatenated into the SQL string, this is a strong indicator of a SQL Injection vulnerability.\",\n  \"citations\": [\n    {\n      \"file_id\": \"F0\",\n      \"line\": 42\n    },\n    {\n      \"file_id\": \"F1\",\n      \"line\": 72\n    }\n  ],\n  \"verdict\": \"LIKELY_TP\"\n}",
